   "name": "cc_contrast",
   "comment": "SURROUND-RELATIVE CONE-OPPONENT CONTRAST -- the eye's centre-surround difference (vision_lateral's lat_pool/lat_residual idiom) generalised to the cone-opponent axes. Per cell: csal = the Euclidean opponent-space DISTANCE of (L-M, S-(L+M)) from its surround mean (a CONTINUOUS contrast MAGNITUDE -- the continuous-in-comparison role of the frame/continuum invariant; the in-frame colour coordinate stays integer), and lsal = the SAME surround-relative difference on the achromatic axis L+M (luminance salience). Reads ONLY raw cone attrs (self + neighbours) -- NO cross-node computed dependency, so firing order is irrelevant. The surround mean is Div(Fold(+neighbour-value), Max(Fold(+1),1)): a TRUE mean that edge-corrects the ring. Flag-gated on ColourParams.salience>0.5, OFF by default (\u00a79). Once per cell (cc_done guard).",
