  {
   "name": "cc_salience",
   "comment": "COMBINE colour salience with luminance salience INTERACTIVELY into Region.residual, which the unchanged vision_stream rule spends a bounded budget over. residual = lsal + (colour armed ? csal + lsal*csal : 0). The interaction term lsal*csal makes a BOTH-channel target's salience NOT a trivial sum (Bauer/Jolicoeur/Cowan reject naive additive-colour); the combine is the parameter-free (1+lsal)(1+csal)-1 -- no magic weight. With colour OFF the residual is lsal alone: colour is ADDITIVE capability, it does not break the luminance path. Flag-gated on ColourParams.salience>0.5 and gated on cc_done (waits for cc_contrast, data dependency). OFF by default (\u00a79). Once per cell (sal_done guard).",
   "match": [
    [
     "scene",
     "has_region",
     "R"
    ]
   ],
   "where": {
    "type": "And",
    "items": [
     {
      "type": "Gt",
      "a": {
       "type": "Attr",
       "node": {
        "type": "PickUnique",
        "source": {
         "type": "NodesOfType",
         "node_type": "ColourParams"
        }
       },
       "key": "salience"
      },
      "b": {
       "type": "Lit",
       "value": 0.5
      }
     },
     {
      "type": "Gt",
      "a": {
       "type": "Attr",
       "node": {
        "type": "Var",
        "name": "R"
       },
       "key": "cc_done"
      },
      "b": {
       "type": "Lit",
       "value": 0.5
      }
     },
     {
